{"text": "Linton Public Adjusters, Inc. — claim file LPA-25-0418\n\nClaim file notes — Okwuchukwu burglary\nInsureds: Ignatius Okwuchukwu and Marisol Okwuchukwu · Loss location: 7218 Pershing Avenue, University City, MO 63130\nCarrier: Hearthstone Mutual Insurance Co. · HO-3 policy HM-MO-7720418-03 · Claim 25-HM-0091844 · Carrier adjuster: Desmond Tarleton, 314-555-0152\nDate of loss: between Oct. 17 and Oct. 19, 2025 (family was away at a wedding in Kansas City)\nPolice: University City PD report no. 25-044187, Det. Aubrey Stiles\nSummary\nBack door forced. Electronics, jewelry and a car taken from the detached garage. Claim was reported online by Mrs. Okwuchukwu on 10/20/2025 at 7:14 a.m.; the carrier's portal log shows the submission came from IP 198.51.100.203, which is the house's own connection. Mr. Tarleton seems to think that is suspicious. It is not; they were home by then.\nContents schedule (Coverage C) — serial numbers supplied by the insureds\nItem\tIdentifier\tClaimed\nMacBook Pro 16-inch (2023)\tSerial C02GK4418MD6\t$2,899\niPad Air\tSerial DMPZ7720Q1GC\t$749\nSony a7 IV camera body\tSerial 4418827\t$2,498\nSamsung phone (old, in a drawer)\tIMEI 355178095580069\t$350\nEngagement ring, appraised 2021\tAppraisal no. GIA-2204418772\t$11,400\nCash in a desk drawer\t—\t$1,200 (policy limit is $200)\n\nVehicle (reported to the auto carrier separately)\n2022 Kia Telluride, VIN 5XYP5DHC4NG204418, Missouri plate RM4 K7T. Keys were on a hook by the back door. Recovered 10/26 in East St. Louis with the catalytic converter cut off.\nCard fraud after the burglary\nA wallet was in the kitchen. Marisol's Visa ending 2996 was used three times on 10/18 ($412.77 total) before the bank froze it; her debit card 4769 15•• •••• 2996 was not used. Expiry on both was 08/27. Not part of this claim, but it helps fix the time of the break-in.\nProblems\nThe carrier has asked for an examination under oath of both insureds on December 3. Their letter cites \"financial motive\": the mortgage is three months in arrears and a foreclosure notice was sent in September. Ignatius says he lost his job at the brewery in June and they are catching up.\nA pawn ticket: Det. Stiles found the camera at Wexler Pawn & Loan on Natural Bridge Road, pawned 10/19 under ticket WX-118204 by a man who gave the name Terrell Okwuchukwu. That is the insureds' 19-year-old nephew, who has a key. They have not told the carrier. I advised them they must, and that I cannot continue if they do not.\nPrior claims: water damage 2019 ($8,300 paid), nothing else.\nFee and next steps\nContract signed 10/22/2025: 10% of recovery, capped per Mo. Rev. Stat. § 375.1007. Estimate being rebuilt in Xactimate for the door and frame. Call both insureds Thursday the 13th — his cell 314.555.0191, hers (314) 555-0107, or marisol.okw@gatewaymail.example.\nShelby Rae Linton, licensed public adjuster, Mo. license PA-8844172 — SRL", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "467 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Ignatius Okwuchukwu", "Marisol Okwuchukwu", "Aubrey Stiles", "Desmond Tarleton", "Marisol", "Ignatius", "Terrell Okwuchukwu", "Shelby Rae Linton"], "companies": ["Linton Public Adjusters", "Hearthstone Mutual Insurance Co.", "University City PD", "Kia", "Gatewaymail"]}, "topics": {"places": ["University City", "Kansas City", "Missouri", "East St. Louis", "Natural Bridge Road"], "health": [], "sensitive": ["Okwuchukwu", "Cleveland", "mortgage", "foreclosure"], "names": ["Ignatius", "Marisol", "Aubrey", "Desmond", "Terrell", "Shelby Rae", "SRL"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 1, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_c